From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:56:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/25] plan9: proc macros as programs (no dylibs on 9front)

A proc-macro crate for a plan9 host is linked as a static program: its
harness adds #[rustc_main] fn main() { proc_macro::bridge::remote::serve(_DECLS) },
rustc lets a plan9 proc-macro crate have an entry and links it as an
executable (its metadata kept, --undefined of the metadata symbol, no
export list). rustc_metadata loads it with bridge::remote::load: the
program is started and says how many macros it has (names and kinds are
in the metadata); their clients carry a remote id. The bridge already
makes every exchange Buffers (handles, strings), as the cross-thread
strategy has it: RemoteStrategy sends the input over the program's stdin,
answers its requests (Dispatcher::dispatch) and takes the output; a
nested run gets a second instance. The program's stdout goes to stderr
(a macro's println! does not break the protocol).

cargo build on 9front: a derive, an attribute and a bang macro of our
own, serde's derive with serde_json (tests/cargo-build.sh).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
